    description: "**Defect.** The `cli_command` entrypoint kind is never emitted despite many argparse-based CLIs, and three other documented entrypoint kinds are also absent.\n\n**Evidence.** `cli_command` is a defined entrypoint-kind enum value (entrypoints.py:157), the lead example in spec §351, and listed in spec §883, but the entrypoint detector classifies 0 symbols with it (kinds present: main_function 11, http_route 8, shell_script 36, script_module 2, html_entry 1, library_export 46) despite dozens of argparse-based Python CLIs under scripts/ — those surface only as library_export/main_function/file entrypoints. The documented kinds cli_command, background_task, connectivity_based, and websocket_handler are all absent from the 104 entrypoints.\n\n**Contract.** The detector should emit the `cli_command` entrypoint kind for command-line tools, as documented.\n\n**Consequence.** CLI tools are invisible as such in the entrypoint inventory; a consumer keying on kind=cli_command to find command-line interfaces gets nothing.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** Same root family as WI-lubap (subprocess linker misses argparse CLIs) but a different surface/producer: the entrypoint detector never classifies any symbol as cli_command."  # 3a98
    fields: {}  # 3a98
