  message: "Done in PR #349 merged to dev @8ccf5b3334 (feature commit 30d22f5f5c + ARCHITECTURE.md regen 9b8a1ec67d). SCOPE REFRAME per wave3_remaining_plan §A ruling: this item's deliverable was re-decided to 'entrypoint-kind as a lightweight catalog-derived axis' (NOT the literal cli_command-emission symptom). DELIVERED (structural evidence): entrypoints.all_known_entrypoint_kinds() (single source = EntrypointKind enum) is registered as the 'entrypoint-kind' axis in multi_value_field_axis._known_axes() (verified: _known_axes()['entrypoint-kind']() returns all 48 EntrypointKind values), mirroring the language/pass-id lightweight catalog axes (ADR-0024 §4); generate-schema now generates the Entrypoint.kind enum from the catalog (removed the phantom 'framework_handler' which was never a real kind; full sorted catalog documented). kind (what the entrypoint IS) and meta.evidence_type (how detected, WI-rukam) are now the two explicit, distinct entrypoint axes. PREMISE RE-VERIFIED (closure-evidence honesty): the original symptom — cli_command/background_task/connectivity_based/websocket_handler absent on the self-corpus (107 entrypoints) — was re-measured live and is mostly dark-for-good-reason: connectivity_based only fires when ZERO concept entrypoints exist (by design); background_task/websocket_handler have no triggering construct in hypergumbo's own code. The genuine cli_command-for-argparse DETECTION gap is NOT fixed by this PR and remains tracked by the sibling WI-lubap (subprocess linker / argparse mis-keying). This item delivers the catalog axis; WI-lubap owns the argparse detector. 100% coverage on all changed files."  # b342
